# 5 Common Wallpaper Mistakes and How to Avoid Them

Wallpapers are a great way to add personality and elegance to any space. Whether you're styling your living room, bedroom, or office, they can make a big visual impact. However, even the most stunning designs can fail to impress if installed incorrectly. At [**Homewall.ae**](https://homewall.ae/), we want to help you avoid these issues. Here are five common wallpaper mistakes—and how to fix them.

## 1. Ordering the Wrong Amount

One of the most frequent mistakes is miscalculating the wallpaper quantity. Ordering too little can cause delays and visible color mismatches when you reorder. This is especially important with printed designs or patterned options like [**abstract wallpaper Dubai**](https://homewall.ae/wallpaper/abstract/), where consistency is key.

**Tip:** Measure each wall accurately and order 10–15% extra to account for cuts and alignment adjustments.

## 2. Misaligned Seams

If seams are off, it can break the visual flow of your wallpaper. Misalignment often happens due to poor leveling or using the wrong adhesive during the application.

**Tip:** Always use a level when applying the first strip. Use the proper adhesive and allow the paper to "book" (rest folded) for a few minutes before installation. This helps keep seams straight and aligned during [**wallpaper installation in Dubai**](https://homewall.ae/services/wallpaper-fixing/).

## 3. Choosing the Wrong Wallpaper for the Room

Not every wallpaper suits every space. A pattern you love for your bedroom may not work well as an [**office wallpaper**](https://homewall.ae/wallpaper/office/) due to lighting, layout, or function. Also, moisture or heavy use can damage delicate materials.

**Tip:** Consider how the room is used before selecting a wallpaper. For high-traffic or humid areas, opt for moisture-resistant or durable materials like textured or vinyl options.

## 4. Poor Wall Preparation

Skipping wall prep can result in peeling, bubbling, or the wallpaper falling off entirely. Even high-quality products won’t stick properly on dusty, uneven surfaces.

**Tip:** Clean and sand the walls as needed. Apply primer and let it dry fully before installation. These steps are essential for a smooth and lasting result.

If you've had a failed attempt, professional [**wallpaper removal**](https://homewall.ae/services/wallpaper-removal/) might be necessary before starting fresh.

## 5. Ignoring Pattern Matching

Wallpaper patterns repeat—and matching those repeats is key to a polished look. Misaligned patterns can look chaotic and throw off the design balance of a room.

**Tip:** Understand the repeat size before cutting. Lay out strips on the floor or wall to preview how the design lines up. This is especially crucial with detailed styles like mural or **abstract wallpaper Dubai**.

